  XsBright: Q([['Why do some stars look brighter than others?', 'They are closer or give off more light', 'They are made of gold|They are painted|They are planets', 'Distance and size affect brightness.'], ['Sirius looks brighter than many bigger stars. Why?', 'It is relatively close to Earth', 'It is the biggest star|It is a planet|It is on fire more', 'Closer stars look brighter.'], ['If two stars give off the same light, which looks brighter?', 'The closer one', 'The farther one|They look the same|Neither shows', 'Brightness drops with distance.'], ['Compared with other stars, how big is the Sun?', 'Medium-sized', 'The largest star|The smallest star|Not a star', 'Many stars are much bigger.'], ['Why can\'t we see stars during the day?', 'The Sun\'s light is much brighter', 'Stars turn off|Stars move away|They are behind the Moon', 'Sunlight outshines them.'], ['What is the closest star to Earth?', 'The Sun', 'Sirius|Polaris|Proxima Centauri', 'The Sun is our star.'], ['Why does a star\'s brightness from Earth not tell you its true size?', 'Its distance also affects how bright it looks', 'All stars are the same size|Brightness shows only colour|Stars are flat', 'A big far star can look dim.']]),
