  XsBike: Q([['Where does a cyclist get the energy to pedal?', 'Chemical energy stored in food', 'Electricity|Sunlight directly|Nuclear energy', 'Food fuels muscles.'], ['At the top of a hill, a cyclist stops pedalling. What kind of energy is highest?', 'Gravitational potential energy', 'Kinetic energy|Sound energy|Light energy', 'Height stores energy.'], ['Why do bike tires feel warm after a long ride?', 'Friction changes some kinetic energy into thermal energy', 'The Sun heats only tires|Air is hot|Rubber makes heat by itself', 'Friction makes heat.'], ['When the cyclist rings the bell, energy is changed into…', 'sound energy', 'light energy|chemical energy|potential energy', 'The bell vibrates.'], ['Pedalling uphill increases which energy?', 'Gravitational potential energy', 'Sound energy|Light energy|Chemical energy in the bike', 'Climbing raises the rider.'], ['What does a bike dynamo light change kinetic energy into?', 'Electrical energy, then light', 'Chemical energy|Sound only|Heat only', 'The dynamo generates electricity.'], ['Why does a cyclist get tired?', 'Chemical energy in the body is used up', 'The bike gets heavier|Gravity stops|The wheels shrink', 'Energy comes from food stores.']]),
